From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 01:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add vendor provider field bridge

Add a source-only bridge that maps the fixed vendor observation records into
an explicitly ordered provider review view.  PPM and cpufreq entries are
reordered by their declared IDs, CSPM remains the fixed four-cluster raw-code
view, and all six EEM detectors are retained while the four canonical bank
IDs are named explicitly.  The real variant, table epoch, and calibration
handle are copied without truncation or synthesis.

The vendor observation ABI does not contain complete policy-limit rows, EEM
voltage units, live clock ownership, or rail conversion.  The bridge records
those omissions as unavailable fields and never presents them as a calibrated
provider.  It is attached only during the explicit vendor lifecycle binding;
it registers no provider, calls no setter, performs no hardware operation,
and admits no CPU.
---
